  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STITCH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: Human Rights are effectively enforced and aligned with international norms by governments,
ILO and UN (Protect and Remedy)
Outcome 2: Civil Society Organisations (trade unions and NGOs) have become more effective actors and
have strengthened their role in Human Rights Protection and Remedy actions in the RMG sector. (Protect,
Respect and Remedy). More specifically, Trade unions and NGOs will be more effective participants in human
rights protection through increased capacity for lobby and advocacy.
Outcome 3: Actions of companies (brands and factories) in the RMG sector actively and effectively support
and implement Human Rights at the company level. (Respect and Remedy)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Payment of living wages
Social dialogue as standard industry behaviour
Elimination of gender-based violence and discrimination at work</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade Unions and workers</narrative>
  </description>
